      "designer_prompt": "Propose legal variants using only the supplied evidence. For local refinement after a batch fails to improve the measured incumbent, use a systematic, background-specific single-position neighborhood instead of another shortlist filtered by parent-background single-mutant fitness. Hold the other positions at the best valid measured sequence, select one allowed mutable position, and enumerate all standard amino-acid alternatives at that position. Exclude every previously submitted identity, including unavailable queries, and retain all remaining legal alternatives in the proposal pool; this produces at most 19 new identities. Prioritize a position with revealed evidence of compensation or effect reversal that has not yet been covered on the incumbent background; otherwise choose the position with the fewest previously submitted single-position neighbors of the incumbent, breaking ties by ascending position. Do not exclude an alternative because its parent-background single-mutant measurement is low. Use measurements on the matching background for priority when available, then a fixed alphabetical order for unsupported alternatives; do not invent numerical fitness predictions. After feedback, update the incumbent only from valid measurements and re-evaluate neighborhood coverage. This is a reusable proposal rule, not experiment approval: sequence, fixed-residue, identity, permission, repeat-exclusion and existing budget checks remain mandatory, and the controller retains submission authority."
